{"case_id": "v4.case.corrected-b03-01", "displayed_text": "If an external agency does not acknowledge your referral, the registered manager should follow the escalation steps: contact the agency’s own duty line to follow up, and if the agency still has not resolved or acknowledged the referral within a further 2 working days, inform the organisation‑level Safeguarding Lead, who may escalate directly within that agency or use the local Safeguarding Adults Board’s escalation route (the post‑referral checklist also instructs following up directly with the agency within 2 working days if acknowledgment is not confirmed). A separate requirement is to complete a post‑referral review within 10 working days of any external referral. \n\nYou must keep a record of the external referral and its post‑referral review outcome in the confidential safeguarding file: every external referral (including to the Office of the Public Guardian or Action Fraud) and its post‑referral review outcome is retained in the confidential safeguarding file in line with the Records Retention Schedule, and safeguarding records are retained for 8 years after the person’s last contact with Alderbridge; these records are stored separately from the general care file with more restricted access. ", "finished_at": "2026-11-13T09:44:55+00:00", "frozen_scope": "primary", "needs_opt_in": ["5323cd6b-8b7a-40f9-98b0-9413c75f643e"], "needs_pipeline_exercised": true, "observation": {"assistant_message_kind": "grounded_answer", "case_id": "v4.case.corrected-b03-01", "contextualisation": {"clarification_question": null, "contextualiser_version": "authorised-user-turns-needs-v1", "interpretation_metadata": null, "resolved_query": null, "status": "resolved", "usage": null, "used_prior_context": false}, "failure_code": null, "generation": {"aspect_links": [{"answer_part_indices": [0, 1], "need_id": "n1", "unsupported_aspect_indices": []}], "aspect_results": {"n1": "supported"}, "generation_fingerprint": "7f1bf6ca0e581fe